        <div id="pothole-depth" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Pothole Depth and How Much Patch to Buy
          </h2>

          <p>
            Depth is the number that decides both which product you need and how many bags to buy, and it is the one most people guess. Measure it properly: lay a straightedge across the hole and measure down to solid material at the deepest point, after you have cleaned out everything loose. A hole that looks 1 inch deep often turns out to be 3 once the crumbled asphalt comes out.
          </p>

          <p>
            Under about half an inch, you are not really dealing with a pothole. Shallow surface wear and small cracks are better handled with a crack filler or a trowel-grade product, because a stone-filled patch cannot be compacted that thin and will ravel at the edges. Between roughly 1 and 2 inches, any of the patches on this list will work, and a single well-compacted lift is usually enough.
          </p>

          <p>
            Beyond 2 inches, place the patch in lifts. Put down about 1 to 2 inches, compact it hard, then add the next layer. A thick patch compacted only from the top stays loose at the bottom, and that loose layer is what lets the whole repair settle into a dish. Holes deeper than about 4 inches should have the bottom filled with compacted gravel first, which is far cheaper than cold patch and gives the patch a firm base.
          </p>

          <p>
            To estimate quantity, work out the area in square feet, multiply by the depth in inches, then divide by the maker's coverage at 1 inch. A 2 by 2 foot hole that is 2 inches deep needs about 8 square-foot-inches of material; with a bag rated at 6 square feet at 1 inch, that is a little over one bag. Always add about 20 percent, because good compaction squeezes the mix down and you want the finished patch slightly proud of the surrounding surface.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">QUICK SIZING RULES</p>
