        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best asphalt patch is the one matched to your hole. For a single pothole you never want to see again, Aquaphalt 6.0 is worth its premium. For several ordinary potholes, EZ Street or QUIKRETE High Performance will do the job at a fraction of the cost, and Latex-ite Quick Patch H2O is the specialist for edges and shallow dips where other patches have nothing to grip.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, the work around it decides the result: clean the hole back to solid material, square the edges, place the patch in thin lifts and compact it until it stops moving. Do that, wait for it to cure before sealing, and a bag of cold patch can outlast the driveway around it.
          </p>
